          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ryobi's snow tools make the most sense as an extension of a platform you already own. The 40V 21-inch single-stage is the standout for paved suburban driveways when bought as a bare tool, the 24-inch two-stage is a premium gas replacement for big jobs, and the 18V ONE+ shovel handles steps and decks for anyone on the smaller system.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Match the tool to your worst storm, match the kit to the batteries in your garage, and keep those batteries warm. Get those three right and a Ryobi will clear your snow without a gas can in sight.
          </p>
